2026-10-27T12:10:52.4843048Z {"at_utc": "2026-10-27T12:10:52.483523+00:00", "operation": "Distinct complete routes share endpoints but preserve different effects", "observation": "Invented rules\nThe strider S takes one or two adjacent steps. Each enemy stone on its chosen route is captured. It can return to its origin. Stones do not move.\nChoose i9, then j10, then i9 to capture and return. The alternative i9 \u2192 h9 \u2192 i9 ends on the same square and leaves the stone intact.\nIf a step can finish now or continue, choose Complete action here to stop at that step. Escape abandons the selection.\nNative acceptance\nVersion 4 \u00b7 Accepted actions 1\nThe native fixture accepted a complete action. Reset to compare another route.\nReset synthetic fixture\nReset starts another temporary demonstration and advances the native version.\nSeparate synthetic record\nTemporary verification data; not a chess document.\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"rules_profile\": \"mshogi.synthetic.strider16.v1\",\n  \"initial_fixture\": \"strider16-capture-and-return-v1\",\n  \"actions\": [\n    \"136>135>136\"\n  ]\n}"}
